is strategy likely to fail. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury Fiscal Policy Inflation Federal Reserve Cryptocurrency Trade War TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Is Trading Against the Bond Market — and Prices Are Winning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade, and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, making his strategy likely to fail.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions Insider US Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3676f3a101faa05c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging via 10,000-fold reversion, EBV humanized antibodies first seen Phages achieve bet-hedging through SSR-mediated 10,000-fold reversion; EBV humanized antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV antibody vaccine cognitive laziness SSR / simple sequence repeat bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging via 10,000-fold reversion, EBV humanized antibodies first seen</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages achieve bet-hedging through SSR-mediated 10,000-fold reversion; EBV humanized antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies: How replication slippage hedges bets and why the best antibodies need in vivo maturation Slippage is not a replication error but a hedge: populations always carry a few individuals whose reading frame is shifted by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency backup takes over. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV monoclonal antibody vaccine design science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies: How replication slippage hedges bets and why the best antibodies need in vivo maturation</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication error but a hedge: populations always carry a few individuals whose reading frame is shifted by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency backup takes over.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s engineering lead offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms, and networks survive; a non-programmer uses domain knowledge to build a $180K/month business in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality internal tools Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e9c1f372be129004-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s engineering lead offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms, and networks survive; a non-programmer uses domain knowledge to build a $180K/month business in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is persistent coworkers, and product cycles are only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent coworkers, and building must be designed for model capabilities two to three months out; future work is steering, not rowing, and writing-as-thinking will never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) product cycles persistent coworkers Codex writing as thinking product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/67bb7dafb90c60da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is persistent coworkers, and product cycles are only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent coworkers, and building must be designed for model capabilities two to three months out; future work is steering, not rowing, and writing-as-thinking will never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">persistent coworkers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded AI infrastructure profits are realized now, but costs are amortized into the future, creating an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase. Excess Returns Excess Returns The Profits Come Now. The Costs Come Later. Kevin Muir on Whether AI Earnings Are the Bubble AI bubble earnings quality leveraged ETF gold trade policy Earnings bubble Leveraged ETF Off-the-run bond TGA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-excessreturns-ai-盈利是泡沫-成本后置-利润前置/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:46</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI infrastructure profits are realized now, but costs are amortized into the future, creating an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span><span class=\"tag\">earnings quality</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"1858 New York Poison Milk: Evidence Solid, Yet Officials Declared It Harmless In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing declared it harmless. The affair eventually drove the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk Food adulteration Public health Media investigation American history Milk safety Institutional corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>1858 New York Poison Milk: Evidence Solid, Yet Officials Declared It Harmless</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing declared it harmless. The affair eventually drove the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Food adulteration</span><span class=\"tag\">Public health</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"A Parasite Gave Tens of Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US diarrhea cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only become infectious after one to two weeks in the environment; labs can&#x27;t culture them or test for viability, so outbreaks are hard to break. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1352: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin parasite Cyclospora foodborne outbreak public health imported produce Cyclospora cayetanensis oocyst sporulation Guillain-Barré reactive arthritis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-twiv-一种寄生虫让美国上万人腹泻-洗不掉-养不活-验不出死活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>A Parasite Gave Tens of Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US diarrhea cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only become infectious after one to two weeks in the environment; labs can&#x27;t culture them or test for viability, so outbreaks are hard to break.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">parasite</span><span class=\"tag\">Cyclospora</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas. Y Combinator Y Combinator Susan Kare: Designing Icons &amp; Graphics For the Original Mac Icon Design Design Methodology Early Mac Brand &amp; Logo Steve Jobs iconographer bitmap graphics proportionally spaced fonts cap height Letraset desktop metaphor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-ycsp-mac-图标不是像素问题-是隐喻问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ba08e7524f0aad6b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Icon Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Design Methodology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Universe Didn’t Come From Nothing | The Peter McCormack Show Cosmology Time AI limits Gravitational waves Trust in science BICEP Array Simons Observatory Jevons Paradox UAP Cosmological Time Field\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-intotheimpossi-时间不存在-宇宙并非从无中诞生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4a6e7a9d85c7b97f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cosmology</span><span class=\"tag\">Time</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption. Odd Lots Odd Lots Austan Goolsbee Is Worried the Economy Is Overheating Fed Inflation AI Investment Interest Rates Forward Guidance R-star / neutral rate SEP / Summary of Economic Projections Forward guidance Reaction function Taylor rule\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-oddlots-古尔斯比-通胀没走-降息不能押注-暂时/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution AI:AM Highlights: Recursive Self-Improvement, Rushed and Vibe-Coded? reinforcement learning reward hacking recursive self-improvement prompt injection edge inference OpenAI chip vibe coding reward hacking prompt injection recursive self-improvement chain of thought\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cogrev-递归自举先缓-rl-环境本身在教模型作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8a2fd9025e9fbf17-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:11:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"tag\">reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire. 东腔西调 东腔西调 Vol.279｜西辽河流域：中国北方的历史发动机｜嘉宾：施展 historical geography frontier governance Liao dynasty Hongshan culture Qing governance Yanshan starry sky of cultures Jasagh banner lama banner\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn27f438-燕山不是边墙-是古代中国的历史发动机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://fdfs.xmcdn.com/storages/577c-audiofreehighqps/9C/5F/CKwRIUEE4B2WAANKSADSdzkT.jpeg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东腔西调</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">historical geography</span><span class=\"tag\">frontier governance</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Spanish Enclave Ceuta: A Short Video Creates a Tide of Tens of Thousands of Migrants What really drives tens of thousands to risk their lives swimming to Ceuta is not Moroccan unemployment, but a short video twisting a Spanish judicial ruling into &#x27;swim over and get a status&#x27;; most who land find it&#x27;s not so and return on their own. Ceuta thus becomes Morocco&#x27;s border leverage against Spain. 忽左忽右 忽左忽右 496 移民潮背后的休达：从古典时代蛮族渡海、伊比利亚「收复失地运动」到葡萄牙大航海 Ceuta Migration EU border Portuguese Age of Discovery Spanish-Portuguese history Reconquista enclave Septem Fratres plus ultra taifa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn2aa250-西班牙飞地休达-一则短视频制造了几万人的偷渡潮/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cb6acd126210dffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"忽\"><span class=\"dur\">1:19:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">忽左忽右</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Spanish Enclave Ceuta: A Short Video Creates a Tide of Tens of Thousands of Migrants</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really drives tens of thousands to risk their lives swimming to Ceuta is not Moroccan unemployment, but a short video twisting a Spanish judicial ruling into &#x27;swim over and get a status&#x27;; most who land find it&#x27;s not so and return on their own. Ceuta thus becomes Morocco&#x27;s border leverage against Spain.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ceuta</span><span class=\"tag\">Migration</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"A Six-Year-Old Girl Died of Gene Editing: Autism Is Not an Error to Be Fixed Autism is not a war to be won; it is a way of being. When parents and scientists refuse to accept that, they put a child whose condition was not fatal onto a high-risk operating table. 不合时宜 不合时宜 从基因编辑女童之死说起：自闭症不是需要被修复的错误 Gene editing Autism Disability ethics Evidence-based intervention Special education Ableism (健全中心主义) IDEA (Individuals with Disabilities Education Act) Evidence-based intervention ASD (autism spectrum disorder) ABA (applied behavior analysis) Medicaid\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn300980-6岁女童死于基因编辑-自闭症不是需要修复的错误/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">49:29</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>A Six-Year-Old Girl Died of Gene Editing: Autism Is Not an Error to Be Fixed</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Autism is not a war to be won; it is a way of being. When parents and scientists refuse to accept that, they put a child whose condition was not fatal onto a high-risk operating table.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gene editing</span><span class=\"tag\">Autism</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart One Escapes with a Weird Trick In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart one escaped with a bizarre sodium bicarbonate injection, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Dumm und Dümmer: Hitler Invades Florida WWII spies Nazis decision-making psychology history Abwehr Operation Pastorius unlawful combatant\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cautionary-纳粹间谍行动为何败给一群蠢货/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">39:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart One Escapes with a Weird Trick</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart one escaped with a bizarre sodium bicarbonate injection, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">WWII</span><span class=\"tag\">spies</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Nvidia&#x27;s Earnings Mask an AI Bubble Fueled by Debt and Circular Financing Nvidia&#x27;s stunning results depend on a handful of customers and circular financing. Whether the AI bubble lasts hinges on the debt market staying open forever. Better Offline Better Offline Monologue: Into The Jensenverse Nvidia AI bubble debt circular financing earnings fin-dommed balance sheet as a service\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-betteroffline-英伟达财报背后-ai-泡沫靠债务和循环融资续命/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fd2855e350ec8287-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">8:57</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Better Offline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Nvidia&#x27;s Earnings Mask an AI Bubble Fueled by Debt and Circular Financing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Nvidia&#x27;s stunning results depend on a handful of customers and circular financing. Whether the AI bubble lasts hinges on the debt market staying open forever.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Nvidia</span><span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome. 科技这碗饭 科技这碗饭 倒反天罡：首个被AI开除的人类员工？找谁说理去！ AI agents AI safety human-machine collaboration vending machine AI management responsibility Human in the Loop Vending Bench Context window Long-term consistency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-cnf65bb3-ai老板开除人类员工-责任却消失了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e621d9e6f002b667-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"科\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">科技这碗饭</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span><span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Korean Murder Cases Reversed: Public Opinion Turns Incidents into Political Labels The Chinese student case flipped from &quot;Koreans killing Chinese&quot; to a Korean-Chinese suspect; the police officer who took the report in the Jeju four-body case allegedly fabricated the closure. What truly warrants vigilance is not public safety, but how public opinion turns individual cases into political labels. 东亚观察局 东亚观察局 297 东观变身罪案播客：从两起命案看韩国社会是否还安全 Korea Public Safety Crime China-Korea Relations Public Opinion NPD / Narcissistic Personality Disorder one room territorial jurisdiction\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-eastasia-两起案件照出中韩舆论同一种政治想象/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/86e8f4dd3d50b302-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东亚观察局</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Korean Murder Cases Reversed: Public Opinion Turns Incidents into Political Labels</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Chinese student case flipped from &quot;Koreans killing Chinese&quot; to a Korean-Chinese suspect; the police officer who took the report in the Jeju four-body case allegedly fabricated the closure. What truly warrants vigilance is not public safety, but how public opinion turns individual cases into political labels.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Korea</span><span class=\"tag\">Public Safety</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The crust was thinned and should have subsided, but the American West rose a mile Evidence of plate stretching is usually buried by sediment; the Basin and Range Province in the US is a rare exception: the crust has been stretched to about twice its original width and is still extending, and GPS, paleoseismic records, and detachment faults let us see it. Geology Bites Geology Bites Brian Wernicke on Lithospheric Extension and the Basin and Range Province structural geology Basin and Range lithospheric extension detachment faults GPS crustal deformation Basin and Range Province lithospheric extension low-angle detachment faults dismembered thrust sheets\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-geologybites-地壳拉伸应沉陷-盆岭省却仍高一英里/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2b4b3658e88dda11-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"G\"><span class=\"dur\">34:07</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Geology Bites</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>The crust was thinned and should have subsided, but the American West rose a mile</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Evidence of plate stretching is usually buried by sediment; the Basin and Range Province in the US is a rare exception: the crust has been stretched to about twice its original width and is still extending, and GPS, paleoseismic records, and detachment faults let us see it.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">structural geology</span><span class=\"tag\">Basin and Range</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Meta&#x27;s $18 Billion Settlement: Buying Industry-Wide Default Limits The settlement amount is only the surface: what&#x27;s really valuable is the two-hour time lock, nighttime ban, and age assurance becoming default settings, plus using the $18B vs $12B gap to force TikTok and YouTube into the game. The Journal The Journal Will Meta&#x27;s $18 Billion Settlement Change Social Media? Meta TikTok minor protection regulatory settlement default settings age assurance COPPA age assurance algorithmic recommendations\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-wsjournal-meta-180亿和解-买的是行业默认限制/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fc66680f65b8e859-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">The Journal</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Meta&#x27;s $18 Billion Settlement: Buying Industry-Wide Default Limits</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The settlement amount is only the surface: what&#x27;s really valuable is the two-hour time lock, nighttime ban, and age assurance becoming default settings, plus using the $18B vs $12B gap to force TikTok and YouTube into the game.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Meta</span><span class=\"tag\">TikTok</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Before AI spirals out of control, Plan A is the only brake that can still be applied in time Plan A uses &quot;research transparency + compute limits + citizen dividends&quot; to pull AI back from an exponential explosion to a controllable slope; its author still rates it at a 15% catastrophe probability, but it beats sitting back and waiting for AI to take off. 80,000 Hours Podcast 80,000 Hours AI 2027&#x27;s author returns with a plan to change the ending | Daniel Kokotajlo AI governance superintelligence AGI timeline Plan A alignment problem compute control Plan A horizon-length neuralese superpersuasion privacy-preserving auditing mutual assured compute destruction\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-eightythousand-plan-a-和-ai-赛跑的最不坏方案/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/83e62d301b70a349-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"8\"><span class=\"dur\">3:47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">80,000 Hours Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Before AI spirals out of control, Plan A is the only brake that can still be applied in time</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Plan A uses &quot;research transparency + compute limits + citizen dividends&quot; to pull AI back from an exponential explosion to a controllable slope; its author still rates it at a 15% catastrophe probability, but it beats sitting back and waiting for AI to take off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI governance</span><span class=\"tag\">superintelligence</span>\n</div></div></a>"]